+/// Where the song is, once the report's track is accounted for. A song change is signalled with
+/// the new `Metadata` and the player's *old* `Position`: MPD (through mpd-mpris) answered 244.00 s
+/// — the previous song's last second — while the title was already the next one, and a scene
+/// counting on from it was four minutes off for the rest of the track. Nothing corrects it either,
+/// because `Position` never signals a move: the next report is the next pause or seek. A song
+/// starts at 0. The first report of a scene keeps the reading, since the scene may be opened
+/// mid-song.
+fn track_position(read: f64, track: Option<String>, last: &mut Option<String>) -> f64 {
+    let changed = matches!((&*last, &track), (Some(prev), Some(now)) if prev != now);
+    *last = track;
+    if changed { 0.0 } else { read }
+}
